# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > b b~ with the order stated: QCD=2.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The stated-order half of the b b~ pair. A group whose default selection is
#     already purely strong is the case where an explicit constraint should
#     change nothing at all, which is worth asserting precisely because it is
#     the case a selector bug would most plausibly survive: the two scripts must
#     produce the same diagram content, and a constraint that quietly dropped or
#     admitted a topology shows up as one count moving.
#
# Not used for amplitudes: no banked b b~ parton row exists (see pp_to_bb).
# The beams read pdlabel = lhapdf with lhaid 247000, for the reason pp_to_bb
# states: MadGraph's internal nn23lo1 default is not an LHAPDF6 grid this
# crate's PDF layer can load.
generate p p > b b~ QCD=2
output pp_to_bb_qcd2 -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  set pdlabel lhapdf
  set lhaid 247000
  done
